
Trading view ICT tools

DeliveryEngine.txt is not mine.
it's from the great Nuno.

Generated files (reminders)
===========================

Run everything from the tvsrc folder. Never edit a generated file by
hand: edit its source and regenerate.

FVGs (source FVGS+IFVG+OTE.txt, i.e. FVGs+IFVG+OTE5):

	python3 tools/mkfvgderiv.py
		writes ICTblocks.txt and FVGS+IFVG+OTE4.txt.
		Markers in the source: //#cut T ... //#end drops the lines
		from derivative T (ote4, blk, or sw for both); //#T code
		keeps "code" only in derivative T.

	FVGS+IFVG+OTE+PL.txt is not generated: apply the same changes by
	hand (it uses dO/dH/dL/dC instead of open/high/low/close).

Levels (source ICTlevels.txt):

	python3 tools/mklevelsderiv.py
		writes ICTgaps.txt and ICTday.txt.

ICTScalp (source ICTScalp.txt):

	python3 tools/mk15.py ICTScalp.txt ICTScalp15.txt
	python3 tools/mkhtf.py ICTScalp.txt ICTscalpHTFFVGs.txt
	python3 tools/mkses.py ICTScalp.txt ICTScalpSes.txt
	python3 tools/mkstrategy.py ICTScalp.txt ICTScalpStrategy.txt

Ports (ICTlevels, ICTcotas and FVGS+IFVG+OTE):

	ninja/<name>.cs and tradovate/<name>.js (FVGS+IFVG+OTE is
	FVGSIFVGOTE) are hand ports. After changing the Pine source,
	port the change and update the source md5 in the port header:

	md5 ICTlevels.txt	(md5sum on Linux)

PDF manuals (doc/), from the doc folder, for each document d:

	t=$(head -1 $d.md | sed 's/^# *//')
	pandoc $d.md -s --css manual.css --embed-resources \
		--metadata pagetitle="$t" -o /tmp/$d.html
	chrome --headless --no-pdf-header-footer \
		--print-to-pdf=$d.pdf /tmp/$d.html

	On the Mac "chrome" is
	"/Applications/Google Chrome.app/Contents/MacOS/Google Chrome".
